Cross-cultural studies of pubertal milestones indicate that these milestones are typically attained around ages 11 to 16 years among boys and 9 to 13 years among girls. Women in most societies tend to report their first sexual experience with men closer to their first menstrual period, but some societies do permit early sexual activity for men and women. However, the average age of sexual debut among young people is much lower than these cross-cultural averages.
