However, these important stages of developing sexuality are not experienced by all people. Some individuals may describe their maturation into sexuality as slow, unexpected, or more gradual than others. On the other hand, some children, particularly males, report that after undergoing puberty, their genitalia do not develop into an adult form. This is called delayed puberty or cryptorchidism.
